Jack Bolsen schrieb:
> 
> I was looking at the high scores at nethack.alt.org and was scratching
> my head trying to figure out how someone managed to amass 2 billion+
> points and in one case over 21 million hit points. Even if you pudding
> farmed, isn't there a limit of 255 kills per pudding type? How is it
> possible to amass some of these scores?

255 is not the limit of kills, it's the limit of what the game will
bother to properly keep track of - '255' just means 'altogether too
many', it can actually represent several thousand kills.

But i think the canonical way to infinite scores is to trap one or
more of the riders on the astral plane behind boulders and merrily
kill them over and over everytime they revive (they always revive,
provided there's at least a single non-occupied grid on the entire
level). For infinite hitpoints, pudding farming is the more likely
approach, because you'll probably need an absurd number of
random-dropped items and sacrifices.

